    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alan-ii-duke-of-brittany">Alan Twisted Beard</a> founded the duchy in 939 after driving the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vikings">Vikings</a> out of Brittany.</li><li>Under the Montfort dukes it built near-sovereign institutions: a council, Estates, a chamber of accounts and its own coinage.</li><li>Defeat in 1488 and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anne-of-brittany">Anne of Brittany</a>’s marriages to two French kings led to union with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> in 1532.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/catholicon-breton-dictionary">Catholicon</a>, a Breton–French–<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latin">Latin</a> dictionary compiled in 1464 and printed at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treguier">Tréguier</a> in 1499, is the first Breton dictionary and one of the earliest of French.</p></aside>
    </section>

